Per 3GPP TS 24.301 (abnormal case j – "UE security capabilities invalid or unacceptable"), the MME shall return an **ATTACH REJECT** message when the ATTACH REQUEST is received containing **invalid or unacceptable UE security capabilities**. Specifically, this condition is triggered by cases such as:

- **No EPS encryption algorithms indicated** (i.e., all bits in the EPS encryption algorithm field are zero);
- **No EPS integrity algorithms indicated** (i.e., all bits in the EPS integrity algorithm field are zero);
- **Mandatory EPS encryption algorithm(s) not supported** by the UE (i.e., the UE fails to indicate support for algorithms that are mandated by the specification, such as EEA0);
- **Mandatory EPS integrity algorithm(s) not supported** by the UE (i.e., the UE fails to indicate support for algorithms that are mandated by the specification, such as EIA0/EIA1/EIA2 as applicable); or
- Other similar conditions where the security capabilities are otherwise malformed, incomplete, or fail to meet network/security policy requirements.

In any of these cases, the MME considers the UE's declared security capabilities as **invalid or unacceptable** for establishing a NAS security context, and consequently rejects the attach attempt by sending an **ATTACH REJECT** message.

Note that the specific **EMM cause value** to be used in the ATTACH REJECT message for this scenario is **not standardized** and is **left up to network implementation** (as indicated in NOTE 2 of the abnormal cases clause), unlike other abnormal cases (e.g., protocol errors) where specific cause values (#96, #99, #100, #111) are mandated.
